# TaIQ job seeder cron schedule
#
# DISABLED here on purpose: scheduling is now driven externally by
# setup_mac_scheduler.sh (macOS launchd), which calls
#   docker compose run --rm job-seeder sh run_seed.sh
# at 2:00 AM local time. Running it both here and from launchd would fetch
# from Adzuna twice a day, which risks exceeding its 250-calls/day free tier.
#
# To re-enable this container's own daily schedule instead (e.g. for a host
# without launchd), uncomment the line below, rebuild, and make sure nothing
# else triggers run_seed.sh on the same schedule:
#   docker compose build job-seeder && docker compose up -d job-seeder

# ┌────────────── minute (0-59)
# │  ┌─────────── hour (0-23)
# │  │  ┌──────── day of month (1-31)
# │  │  │  ┌───── month (1-12)
# │  │  │  │  ┌── day of week (0=Sun … 6=Sat)
# │  │  │  │  │
# 0  2  *  *  *  cd /app && sh run_seed.sh >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
